Boltzmann -- a pipelined-parallel automatic differentiation library.

Named for the step its serial sibling Maxwell does not take.  Maxwell's demon
is one gatekeeper deciding, molecule by molecule, what may pass under an
information budget; Boltzmann is the ensemble -- many identical copies of the
same system considered at once.  Every rank here runs the same program and
they differ only in which partition of the tape each one records.

Jacobians by sparse graph vertex elimination, with the tape partitioned across
MPI ranks: rank r records partitions r, r+p, r+2p, ..., eliminates locally,
and sends the surviving edges one hop around a ring to rank r-1, which merges
them and continues.  The last rank in the pipeline assembles the Jacobian.

  make            build build/lib/libboltzmann.a and every example
  make test       run the whole suite at NP ranks (default 2)
  make ranks      run the assertion suites at 1, 2, 3 and 4 ranks -- the only
                  target that checks the invariant specific to being parallel
  make sanitize   rebuild under AddressSanitizer and run the assertion suites
  make list       every example, with the arguments it runs with
  make clean      remove build/

The layout follows Maxwell's: inc/ headers, src/ the library, examples/ one
directory per example, build/ everything generated and nothing else, and
backup_20260911/ for six examples that predate the checkpointing protocol and
no longer compile.

The public surface is boltzmann.hpp.  See ADAPT-FROM-MAXWELL-2026-09-11.md for
what this library is, how it differs from its serial sibling Maxwell, and
what is outstanding.

READ BEFORE PUTTING MPI IN THE SECTION BETWEEN checkpoint() CALLS: don't.
inc/Typedefs.hpp, beside pass_t, explains why and what would have to change.

Outstanding, from the original README:
